    "specPath": "specs/013-write-gate-and-redaction/spec.md",
    "status": "approved",
    "summary": "Everything that enters the store passes one gate, and the gate runs before the transaction opens. It refuses credentials rather than redacting them, because a redacted secret is still a secret that was transmitted, stored in a log, and possibly embedded. It caps size, requires an establishable origin, and quarantines rather than admits when origin is doubtful. Every refusal is a ledgered Decision with a reason code and never the offending content. The rule set is data, the corpus of fixtures is committed, and the gate is a pure function so its verdicts are reproducible in review.\n",
    "title": "The write gate: refuse secrets, cap size, establish origin, quarantine the rest"
  },
